{"id": "EUVD-2026-108866", "enisaUuid": "6ea9bbba-106a-397c-9857-6277aaae6cd3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Unwind debug trap enable on copy_to_user failure\n\nIf kfd_dbg_trap_enable() fails while copying runtime_info to userspace,\nit had already activated the trap, set debug_trap_enabled, taken an extra\nprocess reference, and opened the debug event file. Return -EFAULT without\nunwinding that state, leaving inconsistent trap state and a refcount\nimbalance that could break later DISABLE/ENABLE.\n\nOn copy_to_user failure, deactivate the trap and undo the rest of the\nenable setup before returning.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/641be20110cdfb6d921605adb42a764a0fccac54", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/656a40bdc20def58790b8512e6000195436d8855", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b39f46eec2f907417d4955bb88434170f94a8d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01112e241e37f9ac98b6f418d93ce2e0b87b7ee0", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98910"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9wgp-44pj-7g49", "CVE-2026-98910"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "019b1e4b-5fdd-349f-83fa-2f66c12d94be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "0eeee9b6-1f3f-3b6e-a854-6a1a9b6fd658", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "3a38b1c4-3f49-338e-a3de-8aab4c150a80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <1b39f46eec2f907417d4955bb88434170f94a8d8"}, {"id": "5fdc0a56-9fba-3a84-93cf-a0432ea5a53b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "77dd1d1c-1bfc-3ae0-952e-f93310fa4c1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}